<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash wheat falls on with Chicago.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash wheat falls on with Chicago.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine cash wheat fell with Chicago Tuesday amid U.S. harvest delays because of rain.</p>
<p>Soybeans, maize and sunflower were also hampered by recent rains in Argentina. Traders said the rains could strengthen prices on existing stocks due to delays in delivery. Prices of new harvests, however, may be weighed down by the impact of the rains.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
